            "options": ["The dog wagged its tail.", "Each of the girls has her own book.", "The team celebrated their victory.", "Everyone should bring their ticket."],
            "correctAnswer": "The team celebrated their victory.",
            "explanation": "While singular 'their' is becoming common, in formal grammar, 'team' is a singular collective noun and should ideally be paired with 'its' (The team celebrated its victory). However, 'Everyone...their' is also debated but widely accepted now."
